docs {
  # v5 Intervention > Associate Staff with Intervention Delivery - [PATH 1]

  Checks that every published intervention links to at least one valid staff
  member responsible for delivering it. Certification accepts one of two paths;
  complete the path your product uses, not both.

  * **PATH 1 (this scenario): Intervention.staffs.** Staff are listed on the
    Intervention's `staffs` collection. Suits products where the same staff
    deliver the intervention to every participating student.
  * PATH 2: StaffCohortAssociation (see the PATH 2 scenario).

  If you choose PATH 1, also run the `[PATH 1]` step of "Recovery and
  Resubmission Scenarios".

  ## Prerequisites

  * "Publish and Maintain Intervention Definitions" completed: the `first`
    Intervention lists two staff after its update (sample: `207288`, `207289`).

  ## Scenarios tasks

  1. __CREATE__ Read the `first` Intervention and confirm it lists at least two staff in _staffs_.
  2. __UPDATE__ the _staffs_ of the `first` Intervention: remove one staff member, keeping at least one.

  ## Scenarios example data

  | Resource                       | Property Name                  | Is Collection | Data Type | Required | Scenario 1: GET | Scenario 2: PUT |
  | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | ------------- | --------- | -------- | --------------- | --------------- |
  | Intervention                   | interventionIdentificationCode | FALSE         | string    | REQUIRED | READ-T2-001     | READ-T2-001     |
  | educationOrganizationReference | educationOrganizationId        | FALSE         | integer   | REQUIRED | 255901          | 255901          |
  | staffReference                 | staffUniqueId                  | TRUE          | string    | REQUIRED | 207288, 207289  | **207288**      |

  Notes:

  * The PUT replaces the `staffs` collection in full, so omitting a staff member removes it.
  * The intervention must keep at least one staff member; removing the last one fails PATH 1.

  ## API response format
  ```json
  {
    "id": "string",
    "interventionIdentificationCode": "string",
    "educationOrganizationReference": { "educationOrganizationId": 0 },
    "staffs": [ { "staffReference": { "staffUniqueId": "string" } } ]
  }
  ```
}
